# SHEYTAN-Local-Agent — build & runtime artifacts
# Source is Go; everything below is generated at build or run time.
#
# ⚠ v1.0.11 LESSON — KEEP THE LEADING SLASHES:
# Runtime data dirs are created NEXT TO THE EXE (repo root in dev). The
# leading "/" anchors them to the repo root ONLY. Without it, the unanchored
# `sessions/` and `sandbox/` patterns ALSO matched internal/sessions/ and
# internal/sandbox/ — the two packages silently never got committed, which
# is exactly what broke the v1.0.9 and v1.0.10 CI builds. A regression test
# (internal/releasegate) now fails the build if a pattern swallows source.
# The same gate runs in GitHub Actions via `go test ./internal/...`.

# Build outputs
/dist-stage/
# /build/ receives GENERATED artifacts (icon-preview.png from gen-syso,
# shot dirs from tooling) — but build/config.yml is committed packaging
# source metadata that CI audits (release-version + workflow grep). Ignore the
# directory CONTENTS, then re-include the one source file. A blanket `/build/`
# is what silently swallowed build/config.yml and broke the v1.1.2 CI runs:
# the file existed on disk, `git add .` skipped it, and GitHub got ENOENT.
/build/*
!/build/config.yml
# 1.1.6 §12: the multi-resolution brand icon is committed packaging
# metadata (regenerated deterministically by scripts/gen-syso).
!/build/sheytan.ico
*.exe
*.syso
*.zip
/local-agent
# v1.11.1 (run 42928792246 residue audit): the retired v1.10.8 local
# Qt-acceptance route (verify-all.mjs + its /sheytan build product) is
# gone — *.exe and /local-agent already cover any local build product.
/build.log
/build1.log

# Runtime data (portable app creates these next to the exe — repo root only)
/models/
/workspace/
/charts/
/sessions/
/logs/
/browser-profile/
/sandbox/
/data/
/config.json
/installed.json

# Test-generated artifacts land under /build/ (covered above).

# Go tooling
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Release staging output (workflow packaging)
/dist/

# v1.1.5: C++ native engine build artifacts (CMake/Make output — the
# shtn-engine-host binary is a build product, never a source file)
/native/engine/build/

# Node frontend dependencies (npm install — root only, never commit)
/node_modules/

# Go module cache/proxies pulled by local tooling
/vendor/

# v1.4.0: browser E2E build products and per-run artifacts (the server
# binary is built by npm run build:e2e; .artifacts holds the isolated
# per-run stacks, traces and screenshots)
/e2e/.build/
/e2e/.artifacts/

# v1.11.1 (run 42928792246 §12): local CI-output directory (the workflow
# writes its persistent step logs here on the runner; a local run of the
# fixture suites or packaging steps produces the same output — never a
# source file). The Qt-host CMake build-tree ignore is retired with the
# Qt host itself: no ui/qt tree exists.
/ci-logs/
